---
import EditorialStaticLayout from '@/components/editorial/EditorialStaticLayout.astro';
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="The Deeper Protocol | Mental Health Content Governance"
  description="The editorial and technical protocol behind Deeper Global's trusted mental health answer engine."
  canonicalPath="/protocol"
>
  <EditorialStaticLayout
    eyebrow="Trust protocol"
    title="The Deeper Protocol"
    lede="Deeper is built to publish mental health answers with traceability, humility, and enough structure to become useful intelligence."
  >
    <h2>1. Structure every answer</h2>
    <p>
      Each answer should map to a question, slug, category, short answer, full answer, source set, review state, risk class, and update date. The current Supabase table is the seed; the v1 architecture makes room for deeper governance.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Classify risk</h2>
    <p>
      Questions involving suicide, self-harm, substance use crisis, abuse, psychosis, medication, diagnosis, or immediate danger require stricter handling and visible crisis support.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Preserve editorial review</h2>
    <p>
      AI can support drafting and structuring, but publication should preserve human editorial accountability and a future path for clinical review.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Build privacy-safe intelligence</h2>
    <p>
      The platform should learn from aggregate topic demand and search behavior without exploiting individual health vulnerability.
    </p>
  </EditorialStaticLayout>
</BaseLayout>
